This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   - Originally: debug why `/api/favorites` sometimes returns 502 and why favorited events later show as unfavorited on the homepage (from a HAR file analysis) — root cause found and fixed in PR #438 (missing `period` query param).
   - Then: plan and implement a new feature to show **past favourites** in a `/preferits/passats` tab, mirroring the existing profile Propers/Passats pattern ("plan the functionality as similar as the past events from a profile"), triggered by discovering (per explicit user instruction "dont assume anything" and "can you test it with the api?") that the backend has NO real cap on favourites, invalidating the original reason `/preferits` auto-pruned expired favourites.
   - Explicit instruction: **"dont commit to develop, create a PR and check the ai suggestions"** (for PR #438, but this practice was carried forward).
   - Explicit instruction: when choosing SDD execution options, user picked **"1"** (Subagent-Driven).
   - Explicit instruction: **"because can we implement faster the implementation with less tasks and less tokens?"** — user then chose **"Switch to inline (recommended)"** from an AskUserQuestion, meaning: stop dispatching separate implementer+reviewer subagents per task for the remaining tasks (11-14); implement directly in-session, still typecheck/test after each change, still self-review the diff, but skip the extra subagent round trips.
   - Explicit instruction: **"create a new pr with everything first"** — prioritize opening the PR immediately over finishing the rest of Task 14's checklist (interrupted mid-verification).
   - Explicit instruction: **"check for ai reviews, ie coderabbitai, etc and fix them if you agree and loop again using ai skill loop review. also we have a big regression that needs to be fixed"** followed by the pasted CI output:
     ```
     Run node scripts/compare-bundle-sizes.mjs --baseline bundle-size-baseline.json --current bundle-sizes.json
     📦 Bundle size regressions detected:
     ERROR /[locale]: 11.14 MB → 11.52 MB (+384.69 KB, +3.37%) (threshold: 10% or 100 KB)
     ERROR /[locale]/preferits: 383.83 KB → 770.19 KB (+386.36 KB, +100.66%) (threshold: 10% or 100 KB)
     Summary: 2 error(s), 0 warning(s).
     ```
     with explicit permission to investigate the bundle-size issue "while you wait for the ai report" (i.e., in parallel with the review loop).
   - Most recent: **"there are a lot of reviews in the PR, check them all"** — user wants a thorough check of ALL review comments/threads on PR #439, not just a quick pass.

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - Next.js App Router, Server Components (RSC), Suspense boundaries, client vs. server component bundling
   - `react-dom/server`'s `renderToStaticMarkup` limitations vs. real Next.js RSC rendering (can't resolve nested async Server Components rendered as JSX)
   - Vitest testing, `vi.mock` path resolution (relative to test file, not the module under test)
   - Turbopack production builds; symlinked `node_modules` breaking Turbopack ("Symlink [project]/node_modules is invalid, it points out of the filesystem root")
   - Yarn Berry (v4) workspace, `.yarnrc.yml`
   - Bundle size analysis: `.next/server/app/<route>/page_client-reference-manifest.js` (300-550KB typical per route in this app), `.next/server/app/<route>/page.js.nft.json`, recursive directory walk bugs in custom analysis tooling
   - Git worktrees (`git worktree add`), SDD (Subagent-Driven Development) workflow: ledger files, task briefs, review packages, fix-loop rounds, scoped re-reviews
   - Superpowers skill suite: brainstorming, writing-plans, subagent-driven-development, using-git-worktrees
   - pr-review-loop skill: CodeRabbit, Cubic, Gemini, GitHub Copilot bot review triggers via `gh api`/`gh pr comment`, GraphQL `reviewThreads` queries, thread resolution mutations
   - i18n: `next-intl`, `getTranslations` (server) vs client-side translation hooks, locale JSON files (ca/es/en) bundled via static import in `utils/constants.ts`
   - React Server Component client-reference-manifests and how Next.js nests child route compiled output inside parent route directories on disk

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`utils/favorites-limits.ts`** (NEW):
     ```ts
     // Deliberately dependency-free: utils/constants.ts imports the full locale
     // JSON files at module scope (~280KB combined), which is fine for the
     // server components that already pulled it in, but FavoriteButton is a
     // client component and importing MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED from
     // @utils/constants there dragged that whole barrel into the client bundle
     // for the first time — +386KB / +100% on /preferits, +384KB on /[locale]
     // (bundle-size CI regression, 2026-07-31). Keep these two here so a client
     // import stays a plain number, not the JSON payload.
     export const MAX_FAVORITES = 10;
     // Authenticated favourites are stored server-side with no real backend cap
     // (verified against esdeveniments-backend/develop — UserFavoriteEventServiceImpl
     // has no count check). This is a client-side-only UX guard, not a real limit,
     // hence the much higher number than the guest cookie cap above.
     export const MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED = 50;
     ```
     Created to fix a real (but not the main) client-bundle regression.

   - **`utils/constants.ts`**: modified to re-export the two constants instead of declaring them, so all existing server-side consumers keep working unchanged:
     ```ts
     export { MAX_FAVORITES, MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED } from "./favorites-limits";
     export const MAX_RESULTS = 15;
     ```

   - **`components/ui/common/favoriteButton/index.tsx`**: import changed from `@utils/constants` to `@utils/favorites-limits` directly (the actual bundle-size fix, since re-exporting alone doesn't help — client code must import the leaf module). Also (from earlier Task 13) contains the soft-limit pre-check inside the onClick handler:
     ```tsx
     if (
       nextIsFavorite &&
       isAuthenticated &&
       favoritesData?.ok === true &&
       favoritesData.favorites.length >= MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED
     ) {
       setIsFavorite(!nextIsFavorite);
       sendGoogleEvent("favorites_limit_reached", { action: "add", max_favorites: MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED, event_slug: eventSlug, event_id: eventId, event_title: eventTitle });
       setLimitMessage(t("maxReached", { max: MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED }));
       return;
     }
     ```

   - **`scripts/analyze-bundles-cli.mjs`**: added new function `getRouteOwnFiles` (route-boundary-aware recursive file walk, stops descending into a subdirectory that has its own `page.js`/`route.js`), used only by `analyzeRouteServerBundle`'s `getAllFiles(serverDir)` call site (changed to `getRouteOwnFiles(serverDir)`). `getAllFiles` (original, fully recursive) is preserved unchanged and still used by `analyzeClientBundles` for `.next/static/chunks/`. Key new code:
     ```js
     function getRouteOwnFiles(dir, fileList = []) {
       try {
         const files = readdirSync(dir, { withFileTypes: true });
         for (const file of files) {
           const filePath = join(dir, file.name);
           if (file.isDirectory()) {
             const nestedPageFile = join(filePath, 'page.js');
             const nestedRouteFile = join(filePath, 'route.js');
             if (
               statSync(nestedPageFile, { throwIfNoEntry: false }) ||
               statSync(nestedRouteFile, { throwIfNoEntry: false })
             ) {
               continue;
             }
             getRouteOwnFiles(filePath, fileList);
           } else if (file.isFile()) {
             fileList.push(filePath);
           }
         }
       } catch {}
       return fileList;
     }
     ```

   - **`bundle-size-baseline.json`**: regenerated via a python3 transform script from the fixed tool's fresh `--format json` output (106 routes now, was 105 — added `/[locale]/preferits/passats`, zero routes lost), preserving `version`/`thresholds` from the old file, updating `generatedAt`/`lastUpdated`/`client`/`clientTotalBytes`/`routes`. Verified previously-inflated numbers corrected: `/[locale]` 11.68MB→408KB, `/[locale]/patrocina` 1.5MB→384KB, `/[locale]/perfil/[username]` 1.1MB→563KB, `/[locale]/sitemap` 1.4MB→383KB, `/[locale]/preferits` 393KB→394.8KB (essentially flat, confirming it never actually regressed).

   - **`app/[locale]/preferits/passats/PastFavoritesAuthGate.tsx`** (NEW, Task 11, implemented inline): Server-rendered gate (no `"use client"`) shown to guests. Fixed a real bug from the plan: used `<h3>` instead of the plan's specified `<h1>`, because `app/[locale]/preferits/layout.tsx` (Task 8) already renders its own `<h1>` — duplicating it would break heading semantics. Comment explains the deviation and cites `NoEventsFound`'s established `<h3>` convention as precedent.

   - **`app/[locale]/preferits/passats/page.tsx`** (NEW, Task 12, implemented inline): Exports `PastFavoritesSectionOrError` (not just uses it internally) specifically so tests can call-and-await it directly, bypassing `react-dom/server`'s inability to resolve nested async components under `<Suspense>`. Key structure:
     ```tsx
     export default async function PreferitsPassatsPage() {
       const [t, authToken] = await Promise.all([getTranslations("App.Favorites"), getAccessTokenFromCookies()]);
       if (!authToken) return <PastFavoritesAuthGate />;
       const activeCount = await countFavoritesByPeriodExternal(authToken, "active");
       const tabItems = buildFavoritesTabItems({ activeCount: activeCount ?? undefined }, t);
       return (
         <>
           <Tabs items={tabItems} active="past" ariaLabel={t("heading")} />
           <div className="w-full mt-section-y">
             <Suspense fallback={<EventsGridSkeleton count={3} />}>
               <PastFavoritesSectionOrError accessToken={authToken} t={t} />
             </Suspense>
           </div>
         </>
       );
     }

     export async function PastFavoritesSectionOrError({ accessToken, t }: { accessToken: string; t: ProfileTranslator }) {
       const section = await FavoritesEventsSection({ accessToken, status: "past" });
       if (section === null) {
         return (<div data-testid="favorites-page-error"><NoEventsFound title={t("errorTitle")} description={t("errorDescription")} /></div>);
       }
       return section;
     }
     ```

   - **`test/preferits-passats.test.tsx`** (NEW, Task 12): Fixed two real bugs found by actually running (not just typechecking) the tests: (1) `vi.mock` path corrected from `"./PastFavoritesAuthGate"` to `"./../app/[locale]/preferits/passats/PastFavoritesAuthGate"`; (2) test 2 rewritten to import and directly call `PastFavoritesSectionOrError` (awaited) instead of going through the full page + Suspense boundary via `renderToStaticMarkup`.

   - **`test/FavoriteButton.test.tsx`** (Task 13): added `isAuthenticatedMock` controllable mock pattern, `beforeEach` reset, and new test `"blocks adding past the authenticated soft limit without calling the API"` — all 4 tests pass.

   - **Files touched earlier (Tasks 1-10, via SDD subagents)**: `utils/constants.ts` (initial MAX_FAVORITES_AUTHENTICATED add), `lib/api/favorites-external.ts` (`listFavoriteEventsByPeriodExternal`, `countFavoritesByPeriodExternal`), `components/partials/period-tabs.ts` (NEW), `components/partials/profile-tabs.ts` (refactored), `components/partials/favorites-tabs.ts` (NEW), `messages/{ca,es,en}.json` (new translation keys), `components/partials/EventsSection.tsx` (NEW, extracted from ProfileEventsSection), `components/partials/ProfileEventsSection.tsx` (refactored), `components/partials/FavoritesEventsSection.tsx` (NEW), `app/[locale]/preferits/layout.tsx` (NEW, plain `<h1>` not HeadingLayout), `app/[locale]/preferits/page.tsx` (full rewrite, split guest/authed branches, Tabs added, FavoritesPageTracker fix), `types/props.ts` (removed orphaned `FavoritesData` interface), `test/favorites-page-auto-prune.test.ts` (updated for no-prune authenticated behavior + tracker coverage), `test/period-tabs.test.ts`, `test/favorites-tabs.test.ts`, `test/favorites-events-section.test.tsx` (all NEW).

   - **`docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-31-favorites-past-events-design.md`** and **`docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-31-favorites-past-events.md`**: committed design spec and 14-task implementation plan.

   - **`.superpowers/sdd/2026-07-31-favorites-past-events/progress.md`**: SDD ledger tracking every task's completion status, fix rounds, and deferred minor findings.

4. Errors and fixes:
   - **Reviewer hallucination (Task 5)**: haiku reviewer's report claimed `en.json`'s `pastTitle` was `"Past favorites - Storbritannien.cat"` (nonsensical Swedish text). I independently verified via `python3 -c "import json; ..."` that the actual file correctly said `"Past favorites - Esdeveniments.cat"`. Documented as a reviewer artifact, not a real finding, in the ledger. **User feedback/self-imposed lesson**: never trust a reviewer's report without independent verification, even when the overall verdict happens to be correct.
